{{Administrative divisions of Guajicutea}}

The '''districts of the Republic of Guajicutea''' are the island state's 16 mainland districtos plus the separate island district of [[Warikú]]. They form the upper local layer beneath the central state and above the municipalities. District governors and district councils coordinate services, regional planning, and Assembly apportionment, while supporting smaller municipalities that cannot manage every service on their own.

